17
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:18,800
That's why writer

18
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:19,700
Marjory Stoneman

19
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:20,100
Douglas

20
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:20,940
called it the

21
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,900
River of Grass

22
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:23,700
in 1947,

23
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,280
the same year

24
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,540
Everglades National Park

25
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,590
was dedicated.

26
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:27,980
But canals,

27
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:29,000
farms and cities

28
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,020
have drained much

29
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:31,000
of it.

30
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:31,560
Today

31
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:32,340
the Everglades is

32
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,340
about half its

33
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:34,530
original size.

34
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:35,480
Now,

35
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:35,880
one of the

36
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:36,880
largest restoration

37
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:37,480
projects

38
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:38,200
in the world

39
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,100
is trying to

40
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:39,800
send that water

41
